<article class="env-lemma" id="0C01">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C01">Lemma <span data-tag="0C01">48.24.6</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(S) =$“$S$ is Gorenstein” is local in the syntomic topology. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\{ S_ i \to S\} $ be a syntomic covering. The scheme $S$ is locally Noetherian if and only if each $S_ i$ is Noetherian, see Descent, Lemma <a href="/tag/034C" data-tag="034C">35.16.1</a>. Thus we may now assume $S$ and $S_ i$ are locally Noetherian. If $S$ is Gorenstein, then each $S_ i$ is Gorenstein by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BVA" data-tag="0BVA">48.24.5</a>. Conversely, if each $S_ i$ is Gorenstein, then for each point $s \in S$ we can pick $i$ and $t \in S_ i$ mapping to $s$. Then $\mathcal{O}_{S, s} \to \mathcal{O}_{S_ i, t}$ is a flat local ring homomorphism with $\mathcal{O}_{S_ i, t}$ Gorenstein. Hence $\mathcal{O}_{S, s}$ is Gorenstein by Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BJL" data-tag="0BJL">47.21.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>